  ],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Creation-Time Identity",
      "items": [
        "Preparing and Split Requested persist before any tmux effect; the invocation budget commits in the same atomic write",
        "The pane starts the unique recorded script: pane_start_command is the primary identity, bootstrap tags are secondary",
        "Once Split Requested is durable, missing tags alone never mean failed; the record stays Unknown until proven or released"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Capacity vs Outcome",
      "items": [
        "Resource state and outcome are orthogonal; an outcome never frees a slot",
        "A slot is freed only by exact-token close, exact inspection proving absence, or explicit user relinquishment",
        "Running, unknown, taken-over, and foreign states all keep counting toward the four-live cap",
        "Automatic close additionally requires the settled outcome and the post-exit shell receipt"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Delivery Outbox",
      "items": [
        "Outcomes persist with delivery pending before send; attempted is persisted after the send",
        "Automatic delivery is at-most-once; notification loss is possible and stated",
        "On reload, pending or uncertain outcomes are displayed for explicit replay, never resent automatically",
        "Task verification stays independent of any reported outcome"
      ]
    }
  ]
}